(kicad_sch
  (version 20230121)
  (generator "eeschema")
  (generator_version "8.0")
  (uuid "518a14f6-88c3-42fc-914b-ea000245c276")
  (paper "A4")
  (title_block
    (title "ledhub-c6")
    (date "2025-01-01")
    (rev "1.0")
    (comment 1 "ledhub-c6 rev 1.0 - WLED 0.15 all-in-one display LED controller (ESP32-C6-WROOM-1).")
    (comment
      2
      "R16/R17 = 0R isolation links: GPIO16 is shared between ENC_B and prog-header TX0, GPIO17 between I2S_SCK and RX0.  Flash firmware via native USB-C (USB-Serial-JTAG on GPIO12/13); for classic UART flashing remove R16/R17 (or hold BOOT while UART is connected)."
    )
    (comment
      3
      "ADC button ladder (GPIO0, 12-bit): +3V3-10k-node; UP=0R->0.000V(0) DN=2.2k->0.595V(738) LF=4.7k->1.055V(1308) RT=10k->1.650V(2048) OK=22k->2.269V(2813) none->3.300V(4095). Thresholds: <369 UP, 369-1023 DN, 1023-1678 LF, 1678-2430 RT, 2430-3454 OK, >3454 none."
    )
    (comment
      4
      "INMP441 is a bottom-port LGA: 0.8 mm sound-port hole in the PCB; reflow recommended (see README).  L/R=GND (left channel), CHIPEN=+3V3."
    )
    (comment
      5
      "LED_5V powers the LED strip only (separate 5.08 mm terminal J4); logic 5 V (+5V) comes from USB VBUS via R20 0R link."
    )
    (comment
      6
      "R21 = 0R series link between GPIO3 (LED_DIN) and 74AHCT125 1A (LED_DINB): keeps the 3.3V MCU domain and the 5V buffer domain on separate nets and allows an optional series damping resistor."
    )
  )
